# Reverse Proxy
A reverse proxy is a server that sits in front of web servers and forwards client requests to those web servers. It acts as an intermediary for requests from clients seeking resources from servers. 

## Example of Reverse Proxy in Nginx
In Nginx, you can configure a reverse proxy by adding the following configuration:
server {
    listen 80;

    server_name example.com;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://backend_server;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }
}